{"level":"beginner","title":"First steps","questions":[{"id":"L1-001","level":"beginner","q":"What is the smallest unit of bitcoin called?","choices":["bitcent","satoshi","finney","wei"],"answer":1,"source":"bitcoin.org developer docs, glossary","q_sw":"Kitengo kidogo cha bitcoin kinaitwaje?","choices_sw":["bitcent","satoshi","finney","wei"]},{"id":"L1-002","level":"beginner","q":"How many sats make one whole bitcoin?","choices":["one thousand","one hundred thousand","100 million","one billion"],"answer":2,"source":"bitcoin.org developer docs, transactions"},{"id":"L1-003","level":"beginner","q":"What does a Bitcoin wallet actually store?","choices":["private keys","paper coins","bank notes","account numbers"],"answer":0,"source":"bitcoin.org, securing your wallet"},{"id":"L1-004","level":"beginner","q":"Who can create a Bitcoin address?","choices":["only miners","only exchanges","only full nodes","anyone, for free"],"answer":3,"source":"bitcoin.org, getting started"},{"id":"L1-005","level":"beginner","q":"What is the title of the Bitcoin whitepaper?","choices":["Bitcoin: Digital Gold for the Internet","Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System","Bitcoin: The Bank Without Banks","Bitcoin: Money Over Email"],"answer":1,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, title"},{"id":"L1-006","level":"beginner","q":"Who wrote the Bitcoin whitepaper?","choices":["Hal Finney","Wei Dai","Satoshi Nakamoto","Nick Szabo"],"answer":2,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, author line"},{"id":"L1-007","level":"beginner","q":"In which year was the Bitcoin whitepaper published?","choices":["2008","2009","2011","2013"],"answer":0,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, 31 October 2008"},{"id":"L1-008","level":"beginner","q":"What is mining in Bitcoin?","choices":["printing paper money","storing coins underground","running a bank server","computers competing to confirm transactions"],"answer":3,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, section 4"},{"id":"L1-009","level":"beginner","q":"What do miners earn for their work?","choices":["only tips in dollars","new bitcoins plus fees","shares in a company","interest from a bank"],"answer":1,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, section 6"},{"id":"L1-010","level":"beginner","q":"What is the maximum number of bitcoins that will ever exist?","choices":["one million","10 million","21 million","100 million"],"answer":2,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, section 6"},{"id":"L1-011","level":"beginner","q":"What is the Lightning Network good for?","choices":["small, fast payments","printing new bitcoins","mining blocks","running banks"],"answer":0,"source":"Lightning whitepaper, abstract"},{"id":"L1-012","level":"beginner","q":"What is a seed phrase?","choices":["a password for email","backup words that restore a wallet","a receipt from a miner","a bank account number"],"answer":1,"source":"BIP-39, abstract","q_sw":"Maneno ya kurejesha (seed phrase) ni nini?","choices_sw":["neno la siri la barua pepe","maneno ya kuhifadhi ili kurudisha pochi","risiti kutoka kwa mchimbaji","nambari ya akaunti ya benki"]},{"id":"L1-013","level":"beginner","q":"How many words are in a common seed phrase?","choices":["4 words","8 words","10 words","12 or 24 words"],"answer":3,"source":"BIP-39"},{"id":"L1-014","level":"beginner","q":"What should you never share with anyone?","choices":["your seed phrase","your receiving address","your wallet name","a transaction id"],"answer":0,"source":"bitcoin.org, securing your wallet","q_sw":"Ni nini usichopaswa kushiriki na mtu yeyote?","choices_sw":["maneno yako ya kurejesha","anwani yako ya kupokea","jina la pochi yako","nambari ya muamala"]},{"id":"L1-015","level":"beginner","q":"What is a Bitcoin address used for?","choices":["mining blocks","sending email","receiving bitcoin","voting"],"answer":2,"source":"bitcoin.org, how it works"},{"id":"L1-016","level":"beginner","q":"What is a transaction fee for?","choices":["paying the wallet maker","paying miners to confirm faster","paying tax","paying the internet provider"],"answer":1,"source":"bitcoin.org, FAQ"},{"id":"L1-017","level":"beginner","q":"What happens when you send bitcoin to the wrong address?","choices":["it bounces back","the bank returns it","a miner fixes it","it is lost"],"answer":3,"source":"bitcoin.org, FAQ","q_sw":"Ukituma bitcoin kwa anwani isiyo sahihi, nini hutokea?","choices_sw":["inarudi","benki inairudisha","mchimbaji anairekebisha","inapotea"]},{"id":"L1-018","level":"beginner","q":"What is the blockchain?","choices":["a public record of confirmed transactions","a private bank database","a list of miners","an email archive"],"answer":0,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, section 3"},{"id":"L1-019","level":"beginner","q":"What is a block?","choices":["a kind of wallet","a mining computer","a bundle of confirmed transactions","a secret code"],"answer":2,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, section 3"},{"id":"L1-020","level":"beginner","q":"About how often is a new block found?","choices":["every 10 seconds","about every 10 minutes","once a day","once a week"],"answer":1,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, section 4"},{"id":"L1-021","level":"beginner","q":"What is the Lightning Network?","choices":["a fast payment layer on top of Bitcoin","a new coin replacing bitcoin","a mining company","a bank network"],"answer":0,"source":"Lightning whitepaper, abstract"},{"id":"L1-022","level":"beginner","q":"What does a Lightning invoice state?","choices":["a block height","a miner name","a dollar bill","an amount to pay"],"answer":3,"source":"BOLT 11"},{"id":"L1-023","level":"beginner","q":"What are QR codes used for in Bitcoin?","choices":["mining blocks faster","sharing an address or invoice easily","hiding a wallet","printing paper money"],"answer":1,"source":"BIP-21"},{"id":"L1-024","level":"beginner","q":"What do confirmations mean?","choices":["emails from miners","votes from banks","blocks added after your transaction","receipts from shops"],"answer":2,"source":"bitcoin.org, FAQ","q_sw":"Uthibitisho (confirmation) maana yake nini?","choices_sw":["barua kutoka kwa wachimbaji","kura kutoka kwa benki","vitalu vilivyoongezwa baada ya muamala wako","risiti kutoka madukani"]},{"id":"L1-025","level":"beginner","q":"What is a full node?","choices":["a computer that checks every Bitcoin rule","a big mining farm","a bank branch","a coin shop"],"answer":0,"source":"bitcoin.org, full node guide"},{"id":"L1-026","level":"beginner","q":"Is Bitcoin run by a company?","choices":["yes, by Bitcoin Inc.","no, by nobody central","yes, by the miners union","yes, by Satoshi's company"],"answer":1,"source":"bitcoin.org, FAQ"},{"id":"L1-027","level":"beginner","q":"What is a halving?","choices":["the price halves","miners stop","the block reward halves about every 4 years","wallets split in two"],"answer":2,"source":"bitcoin.org, FAQ"},{"id":"L1-028","level":"beginner","q":"What was the first block reward?","choices":["50 BTC per block","5 BTC per block","1 BTC per block","100 BTC per block"],"answer":0,"source":"Bitcoin whitepaper, section 6","q_sw":"Zawadi ya kwanza kwa kila block ilikuwa kiasi gani?","choices_sw":["BTC 50 kwa kila block","BTC 5 kwa kila block","BTC 1 kwa kila block","BTC 100 kwa kila block"]},{"id":"L1-029","level":"beginner","q":"What is the genesis block?","choices":["the biggest block","the last block","a lost wallet","the first block of Bitcoin"],"answer":3,"source":"bitcoin.org, glossary"},{"id":"L1-030","level":"beginner","q":"What message sits in the genesis block?","choices":["hello world","a bank bailout headline from The Times","a miner's name","a prayer"],"answer":1,"source":"Genesis block coinbase"},{"id":"L1-031","level":"beginner","q":"Which code stands for bitcoin on exchanges?","choices":["BTN","XBC","BTC","BCC"],"answer":2,"source":"bitcoin.org, FAQ"}]}
